Vincent Fecteau's eight painted sculptures at the Art Institute of Chicago are so personal that their achievement often looks indistinguishable from eccentricity. Little in modern sculpture prepares you for them, so you hunt for resemblances to models for contemporary architecture or design -- not being satisfied there either.
